{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/257702-the-mystery-dot","id":257702,"title":"The Mystery Dot...!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-15T17:21:45-07:00","id":257702,"title":"The Mystery Dot...!","content":"First off, read this blog post about an excellent charity: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-saved-against-fear-this-weekend/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/i-saved-again...-this-weekend/</a><br /> <br /> Now look at the bottom of the development updates. Right down there. At the very end. What do you see?<br /> <br /> ...That's right. It's a &quot;Fill In the Blank&quot; dot. It could be anything.<br /> <br /> LET THE WILD SPECULATION COMMENCE!!! <hr />I really hope it's <b>Blood: The Bloodening</b>, where you play a blood cell. OP &amp; WW have been teasing this forever, since Masquerade! Why else would Blood play such an important role in Vampire, Werewolf, AND Mage? Think about it: all the characters you've played have Blood, or did at one time (don't think you can get out of this so easily, Wraith!)!<br /> <br /> I could totally see an axis where you play as a TYPE of blood cell -- like a platelet or a red blood cell or a white blood cell or maybe some plasma -- and you have to figure out what happens when suddenly <b>The Bloodening</b> happens!<br /> <br /> Just what is <b>The Bloodening</b>? How does your character react to it? What does it do to your Cel (the name for a group of blood cells)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":".  more ludicrosity 09-15-2014, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T00:52:08-07:00","id":257965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/257702-the-mystery-dot#post257702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, read this blog post about an excellent charity: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-saved-against-fear-this-weekend/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/i-saved-again...-this-weekend/</a><br /> <br /> Now look at the bottom of the development updates. Right down there. At the very end. What do you see?<br /> <br /> ...That's right. It's a &quot;Fill In the Blank&quot; dot. It could be anything.<br /> <br /> LET THE WILD SPECULATION COMMENCE!!! <hr />I really hope it's <b>Blood: The Bloodening</b>, where you play a blood cell. OP &amp; WW have been teasing this forever, since Masquerade! Why else would Blood play such an important role in Vampire, Werewolf, AND Mage? Think about it: all the characters you've played have Blood, or did at one time (don't think you can get out of this so easily, Wraith!)!<br /> <br /> I could totally see an axis where you play as a TYPE of blood cell -- like a platelet or a red blood cell or a white blood cell or maybe some plasma -- and you have to figure out what happens when suddenly <b>The Bloodening</b> happens!<br /> <br /> Just what is <b>The Bloodening</b>? How does your character react to it? What does it do to your Cel (the name for a group of blood cells)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bloodening is what the cells call it when they bleed from the body, or are sucked out by a syringe/Vampire. The story of the game is your Cel struggling to survive in the outside world/inside a Vampire, using their powers - Stigmata.<br /> <br /> The energy stat is 'Oxygen'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}